# Meeting-pipeline crontab TEMPLATE for a per-jurisdiction Lightsail box.
# Rendered by provision-jurisdiction.sh (__SLUG__ -> the jurisdiction slug)
# and installed with `crontab <rendered file>` as the `ubuntu` user. The
# LFUCG reference box keeps its hand-written deploy/lightsail/crontab.txt.
#
# Box TZ:   sudo timedatectl set-timezone America/New_York
#           (cron honors the system TZ; ET keeps the schedule aligned to
#            when the portal posts clips, and DST is handled automatically)
#
# LOGS -> /var/log/fuzzy-potato/ (a dir OWNED BY ubuntu). Do NOT log straight
# into /var/log — it is root:syslog, so the `ubuntu` user cannot CREATE a new
# file there and cron's `>>` redirect fails to OPEN before flock runs, silently
# skipping the job. Provision once (both the LFUCG box and every jurisdiction):
#   sudo mkdir -p /var/log/fuzzy-potato && sudo chown ubuntu:ubuntu /var/log/fuzzy-potato
# Rotation/compression: install deploy/lightsail/logrotate-fuzzy-potato into
# /etc/logrotate.d/. Log FILENAMES stay per-slug so co-located boxes never collide.
#
# All jobs share one flock so a long catch-up run can never overlap the next
# tick or the weekly backfill. `-n` skips this firing if the lock is held;
# `-E 99` makes flock return a DISTINCT exit code (99) on that lock-contended
# skip so we can tell "skipped" apart from "the job ran and FAILED". Each line
# captures flock's exit code and:
#   rc == 0   -> SUCCESS -> ping the success heartbeat (CloudWatch LT/Heartbeat)
#   rc == 99  -> SKIPPED -> ping nothing (a rare skip is covered by the next run;
#                          a whole missed window still trips the dead-man alarm)
#   otherwise -> FAILED  -> ping a DISTINCT __SLUG__-<job>-fail metric, NEVER the
#                          success one. main.py exits non-zero when the search.db
#                          build / RAG ingest / index generation fail, so a broken
#                          run can no longer masquerade as healthy. (Wire an alarm
#                          on lt-heartbeat-__SLUG__-<job>-fail >0 for failure paging.)
# The weekly index backup self-heartbeats from inside the script after the S3
# upload, so its cron line has no appended ping.
#
# IMPORTANT (cold-start gate, spec §2.6): do NOT install this crontab until
# the one-time cold-start backfill has finished. Lean + bulk runs fighting
# over search.db / ChromaDB during the initial archive sweep is the failure
# mode the flock can't prevent (different scripts, same data dir).
#
# Provisioning note: document-driven jurisdictions (CivicClerk, e.g. Paris)
# install ingest + daily summaries + weekly index backup + telemetry prune and
# OMIT the weekly backfill line (backfill-docs / tables-of-motions are Granicus-
# packet specific). Granicus jurisdictions install all of them.
#
# Lean incremental ingest — every 6h, EVERY day at 02:00/08:00/14:00/20:00 ET.
# (Was weekdays-only [1-5]; a no-new-clip run exits in seconds, and skipping
# weekends delayed weekend/Friday-evening clips by up to ~54h.)
# probe -> process new clips -> RAG ingest -> reload API -> S3 + CF + feeds
0 2,8,14,20 * * *  /usr/bin/flock -n -E 99 /tmp/__SLUG__-pipeline.lock /opt/fuzzy-potato/deploy/lightsail/ingest_cron.sh >> /var/log/fuzzy-potato/__SLUG__-ingest.log 2>&1; rc=$?; if [ "$rc" -eq 0 ]; then /opt/fuzzy-potato/deploy/lightsail/heartbeat.sh __SLUG__-ingest; elif [ "$rc" -ne 99 ]; then /opt/fuzzy-potato/deploy/lightsail/heartbeat.sh __SLUG__-ingest-fail; fi

# Daily v2-summary upgrade — every day at 00:00 ET. Generates the two-pass
# summary + facts for clips the lean ingest deferred, re-ingests + refreshes.
0 0 * * *  /usr/bin/flock -n -E 99 /tmp/__SLUG__-pipeline.lock /opt/fuzzy-potato/deploy/lightsail/summaries_cron.sh >> /var/log/fuzzy-potato/__SLUG__-summaries.log 2>&1; rc=$?; if [ "$rc" -eq 0 ]; then /opt/fuzzy-potato/deploy/lightsail/heartbeat.sh __SLUG__-summaries; elif [ "$rc" -ne 99 ]; then /opt/fuzzy-potato/deploy/lightsail/heartbeat.sh __SLUG__-summaries-fail; fi

# Heavy archive-wide sweeps — weekly, Sunday 03:00 ET. (Granicus only — omit
# on document-driven boxes.) backfill-docs + tables-of-motions, then reload.
0 3 * * 0  /usr/bin/flock -n -E 99 /tmp/__SLUG__-pipeline.lock /opt/fuzzy-potato/deploy/lightsail/backfill_weekly.sh >> /var/log/fuzzy-potato/__SLUG__-backfill.log 2>&1; rc=$?; if [ "$rc" -eq 0 ]; then /opt/fuzzy-potato/deploy/lightsail/heartbeat.sh __SLUG__-backfill; elif [ "$rc" -ne 99 ]; then /opt/fuzzy-potato/deploy/lightsail/heartbeat.sh __SLUG__-backfill-fail; fi

# Weekly off-box index backup — Sunday 04:30 ET. tars vec.db + search.db +
# rag_state.json (+ chroma_db + state.json where they exist) to S3.
# Self-heartbeats __SLUG__-index-backup.
30 4 * * 0  /usr/bin/flock -n -E 99 /tmp/__SLUG__-pipeline.lock /opt/fuzzy-potato/deploy/lightsail/backup_indexes.sh >> /var/log/fuzzy-potato/__SLUG__-backup.log 2>&1

# Weekly telemetry retention prune — Sunday 05:00 ET. Deletes rag_events older
# than 90 days from lfucg_output/telemetry.db, then wal_checkpoint(TRUNCATE).
# Best-effort (never raises). No pipeline flock — telemetry.db is a separate WAL
# sqlite and prune_old_events is concurrency-safe.
0 5 * * 0  cd /opt/fuzzy-potato && set -a && . ./.env && set +a && /home/ubuntu/.local/bin/uv run python -c "from rag.telemetry import prune_old_events; print('telemetry rows pruned:', prune_old_events(90))" >> /var/log/fuzzy-potato/__SLUG__-telemetry-prune.log 2>&1
